<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Jan 20.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Jan 20.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended Jan 18</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE    % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				 (RS MLN)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>State Bank	   280	   2.08     453300 126.92    38.73</p>
<p>Reliance	     240	   1.81     359450  86.27    39.32</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   190	   1.42     365300  69.41    38.97</p>
<p>Tata Engg	    335	   2.65     179900  60.27    41.25</p>
<p>ITC		    395	   2.29     109900  43.13    30.23</p>
<p>L&amp;T		    245	   1.93     141250  34.61    41.08</p>
<p>MTNL		   235	   1.94     146300  34.38    43.05</p>
<p>Tata Power	   135	   1.04     208550  28.15    40.17</p>
<p>BSES		   220	   1.17     115500  25.41    27.73</p>
<p>ACC		   1420	  10.11	17390  24.69    37.12</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 38.15 percent on an annualised basis against 17.84 percent in the previous carry forward account ended Jan 11.</p>
